Migrations 002-027 shipped, were applied everywhere, and their files were
deleted in ab902af2 when the declarative schema in ../ plus seeds became the
bootstrap for a fresh install.

Every database created before that commit still carries a tracking row for each
of these numbers. Refilling one would leave the new SQL unexecuted and the boot
refusing on a checksum that belongs to a migration nobody can find, so the span
is recorded here and the build rejects any file that claims it.

Nothing here is executed. This file exists so that `ls` tells the truth about
which numbers are free.
